#=GF RN [1]
#=GF RM 10893274
#=GF RT Fibroblast growth factor 2 internal ribosome entry site (IRES) activity ex
#=GF RT vivo and in transgenic mice reveals a stringent tissue-specific
#=GF RT regulation.
#=GF RA Creancier L, Morello D, Mercier P, Prats AC
#=GF RL J Cell Biol 2000;150:275-281.
#=GF RN [2]
#=GF RM 7799942
#=GF RT Alternative translation of human fibroblast growth factor 2 mRNA occurs by
#=GF RT internal entry of ribosomes.
#=GF RA Vagner S, Gensac MC, Maret A, Bayard F, Amalric F, Prats H, Prats AC
#=GF RL Mol Cell Biol 1995;15:35-44.
#=GF CC This family represents the fibroblast growth factor 2 (FGF-2) internal
#=GF CC ribosome entry site (IRES). When expressed the FGF-2 protein plays a
#=GF CC pivotal role in cell proliferation, differentiation and survival as well
#=GF CC as being involved in wound-healing [1,2]. It has been found that FGF-2
#=GF CC IRES activity is strictly controlled and highly tissue specific. It is
#=GF CC thought that translational IRES dependent activation of FGF-2 plays a
#=GF CC vital role in embryogenesis and in the adult brain [1].
#=GF WK FGF-2_internal_ribosome_entry_site_(IRES)
#=GF SQ 6

